Meta-Narrative: The Toad's Legacy
At the bottom of a summer pond, a toad rests in still water, releasing bubbles from its mouth. Each bubble rises, expands, deforms, oscillates, and ultimately ruptures, returning to the water.
Within this image:
•	The water is the substrate — the unseen, all-bearing ground.
•	The bubble wall is the cosmic membrane — ordered structure emergent from the substrate.
•	The bubble's ascent is time — irreversible unfolding.
•	The bubble's expansion is the cooling and evolution of the cosmos.
•	The bubble's texture is matter — woven configurations upon the membrane.
•	The bubble's rupture is the end — structural dissolution, return to the substrate.
Intuitive Dynamical Image: An unbounded vat of dense liquid substrate, driven by internal statistical fluctuations (ensemble fluctuations of local reconnection event rates), attains a critical phase transition threshold, generating an expanding and ultimately dissipating topological bubble. This is the universe.
The toad's bubble-blowing is the starting point of my model. Through multiple rounds of iterative refinement, I cannot abandon it. Without this imagery, none of this would exist. I therefore continue to call it the Toad Universe Model. I also prefer to call my topological stars Toad Stars.
Epigraph for Part XI: Meaning is not conserved; only reconnection endures.
