Throughout this work, everyday physical terms — "cooling," "heating," "radiation," "temperature," "pressure," "energy," "mass," "force" — retain their phenomenological descriptive function. Their microscopic first-principle definitions within the TDMU framework correspond strictly to geometric quantities: loop density variations, shared link density gradients, transverse/longitudinal wave modes, shared link compressive stress, reconnection step counts, and topological charge differences.
