General relativity is the macroscopic continuum limit of TDMU when two conditions are simultaneously satisfied:
1.	Membrane loop density is sufficiently high — topological knot count N→∞N→∞, total shared link count Ntotal→∞Ntotal→∞;
2.	Observational scale greatly exceeds the recursive cutoff radius — L≫κ⋅rAL≫κ⋅rA (Corollary 3.1).
