•	"Geodesic deviation" in general relativity is the relative shift of two shortest paths in the shared link network under the statistical limit.
•	"Singularity" in general relativity has no existence in TDMU — it is replaced by the connection-saturated state, a finite-density, finite-curvature geometric limit.
Status Determination:
