•	Solar system scales (phenomenologically r∼1010r∼1010 m)
•	Galactic scales (phenomenologically r∼1020r∼1020 m)
•	Any local membrane region with high loop density and high recursive order
Beyond this domain — such as during global membrane phase transitions or regimes dominated by discrete topological knot exchange — general relativity fails, and TDMU supersedes it.
