•	The "vacuum" in quantum field theory is the membrane ground state with non-zero loop density below critical threshold, not an empty spacetime.
Status Determination:
Quantum field theory (including the Standard Model) is an effective approximation of TDMU in the low-energy, weak-interaction limit, applicable to:
•	Particle physics (MeV–TeV scales)
•	Condensed matter physics (low temperature, low energy)
•	Any local membrane region where topological knot exchange statistics dominate but global Path-II reconnection has not yet triggered
Beyond this domain — such as during membrane emergence phase transitions, connection-saturated states, or global Path-II triggered states — quantum field theory fails, and TDMU supersedes it.
